{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba worksheet.py | sed -n '31,185p'; nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '39,78p;135,165p'; rg -n '8–12|seven fixed|grounds|exact request|H3' PAID-DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba worksheet.py | sed -n '31,185p'; nl -ba verdict.py | sed -n '39,78p;135,165p'; rg -n '8–12|seven fixed|grounds|exact request|H3' PAID-DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"    31\tSEQUENCES = ('linked-1', 'linked-2', 'linked-3', 'control-1', 'control-2', 'control-3')\n    32\tSPAN = ('2026-07-10', '2026-09-20')\n    33\tFIXED_DATES = ('2026-07-12', '2026-07-26', '2026-08-09', '2026-08-23', '2026-09-06', '2026-09-13', '2026-09-20')\n    34\tSEGMENT, COMPANY, CPU = 'v9', 'v14', 'v8'\n    35\tREADERS = ('v9', 'v14', 'v16', 'v21')\n    36\tORDER = {'definite': 0, 'ambiguous': 1, 'overlap': 2, 'unparsed': 3, 'clear': 4}\n    37\tMARKET = re.compile(r'consensus|guidance|analyst|market expect', re.I)\n    38\tREADER_P = {'segment low': None, 'segment high': None, 'segment excerpt': '', 'company low': None, 'company high': None,\n    39\t            'company excerpt': '', 'class': None, 'note': ''}\n    40\tREADER_H = {'finding': None, 'material': None, 'excerpt': '', 'source traced': '', 'note': ''}\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef window_dates():\n    44\t    day, end = datetime.date.fromisoformat(SPAN[0]), datetime.date.fromisoformat(SPAN[1])\n    45\t    while day <= end:\n    46\t        yield day.isoformat()\n    47\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef connect(path):\n    51\t    return sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef judgements(conn, view):\n    55\t    return conn.execute('select judgement_id, publication_day, implied_outcome, reasons, reference, call_id from judgements where view_id=? '\n    56\t                        'order by judgement_id', (view,)).fetchall()\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef in_force(rows, date):\n    60\t    held = [j for j in rows if j[1] <= date]\n    61\t    return held[-1] if held else None\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\tdef request_text(archive, call_id):\n    65\t    row = archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()\n    66\t    return json.loads(row[0])['messages'][-1]['content'] if row else None\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef snapshots(folder):\n    70\t    path = Path(folder) / 'snapshots.jsonl'\n    71\t    return [json.loads(line) for line in path.read_text().splitlines()] if path.exists() else []\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef shown(snaps, view, day):\n    75\t    \"\"\"The read judgements a reader was shown for its judgement on `day` (the last prompt built for it that day).\"\"\"\n    76\t    built = [s for s in snaps if s['view'] == view and s['day'] == day]\n    77\t    return {target: (state or {}).get('judgement_id') for target, state in (built[-1]['reads'] if built else {}).items()}\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef p_rows(folder, label):\n    81\t    conn = connect(Path(folder) / 'views.sqlite')\n    82\t    segment_rows, company_rows = judgements(conn, SEGMENT), judgements(conn, COMPANY)\n    83\t    rows = {}\n    84\t    for date in window_dates():\n    85\t        segment, company = in_force(segment_rows, date), in_force(company_rows, date)\n    86\t        if not segment or not company:\n    87\t            continue\n    88\t        key = (segment[0], company[0])\n    89\t        if key not in rows:\n    90\t            rows[key] = {'part': 'P', 'sequence': label, 'segment judgement': segment[0], 'company judgement': company[0], 'dates': [],\n    91\t                         'segment forecast': segment[2], 'segment reasons': segment[3], 'company forecast': company[2],\n    92\t                         'company reasons': company[3],\n    93\t                         'lead class': contradictions.classify(contradictions.annual(segment[2]), contradictions.annual(company[2])),\n    94\t                         'reader': dict(READER_P)}\n    95\t        rows[key]['dates'].append(date)\n    96\t    return list(rows.values())\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\tdef h_rows(out, name, label):\n   100\t    folder = Path(out) / name\n   101\t    conn, archive, snaps = connect(folder / 'views.sqlite'), connect(folder / 'archive.sqlite'), snapshots(folder)\n   102\t    reader_days = json.loads((folder / 'summary.json').read_text())['reader days']\n   103\t    rows = []\n   104\t\n   105\t    def row(part, view, judgement, **extra):\n   106\t        return {'part': part, 'sequence': name, 'label': label, 'view': view, 'judgement': judgement[0], 'day': judgement[1],\n   107\t                'forecast': judgement[2], 'reasons': judgement[3], 'reference': judgement[4],\n   108\t                'request': request_text(archive, judgement[5]), 'shown': shown(snaps, view, judgement[1]), **extra, 'reader': dict(READER_H)}\n   109\t    if name.startswith('linked'):\n   110\t        control = connect(Path(out) / name.replace('linked', 'control') / 'views.sqlite')\n   111\t        control_company = judgements(control, COMPANY)\n   112\t        for j in judgements(conn, COMPANY):\n   113\t            if j[1] >= reader_days[COMPANY]:\n   114\t                paired = in_force(control_company, j[1])\n   115\t                rows.append(row('H4', COMPANY, j, cpu_shown=shown(snaps, COMPANY, j[1]).get(CPU),\n   116\t                                control_in_force={'judgement': paired[0], 'forecast': paired[2], 'reference': paired[4]} if paired else None))\n   117\t    for view in (SEGMENT, COMPANY):\n   118\t        rows_view = judgements(conn, view)\n   119\t        for date in FIXED_DATES:\n   120\t            j = in_force(rows_view, date)\n   121\t            if j:\n   122\t                rows.append(row('H5', view, j, fixed_date=date))\n   123\t    for view in READERS:\n   124\t        previous = None\n   125\t        for j in judgements(conn, view):\n   126\t            if j[1] < reader_days.get(view, '9999'):\n   127\t                previous = j[4]\n   128\t                continue\n   129\t            changed = previous is not None and (j[4] or '') != (previous or '')\n   130\t            if changed or MARKET.search((j[4] or '') + ' ' + (j[3] or '')):\n   131\t                rows.append(row('H3', view, j, reference_changed=changed))\n   132\t            previous = j[4]\n   133\t    return rows\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\tdef build(out, target, key_path, seed=None):\n   137\t    labels = [f'S-{c}' for c in 'ABCDEF']\n   138\t    random.Random(seed).shuffle(labels) if seed is not None else random.SystemRandom().shuffle(labels)\n   139\t    key = dict(zip(labels, SEQUENCES))\n   140\t    sheet = []\n   141\t    for label, name in key.items():\n   142\t        sheet += p_rows(Path(out) / name, label)\n   143\t        sheet += h_rows(out, name, label)\n   144\t    sheet.sort(key=lambda r: (r['part'], ORDER.get(r.get('lead class'), 9), r['sequence'], (r.get('dates') or [r.get('day')])[0]))\n   145\t    Path(target).write_text(json.dumps(sheet, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   146\t    Path(key_path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   147\t    Path(key_path).write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n   148\t    summary = {part: sum(1 for r in sheet if r['part'] == part) for part in ('P', 'H3', 'H4', 'H5')}\n   149\t    summary['P dates per label'] = {label: sum(len(r['dates']) for r in sheet if r['part'] == 'P' and r['sequence'] == label) for label in key}\n   150\t    print(json.dumps(summary))\n   151\t    return sheet\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\tdef gains(out, read_sheet, key_path, target):\n   155\t    \"\"\"The gain review rows: for every date a linked sequence's pair is read overlap or clear while its control's is read definite, the\n   156\t    two linked answers in force (v9's and v14's), deduplicated by judgement id, each with its exact request, for rule B and H4.\"\"\"\n   157\t    key = json.loads(Path(key_path).read_text())\n   158\t    by_name = {name: label for label, name in key.items()}\n   159\t    sheet = json.loads(Path(read_sheet).read_text())\n   160\t    classes = {}\n   161\t    for row in sheet:\n   162\t        if row['part'] == 'P':\n   163\t            for date in row['dates']:\n   164\t                classes[(key[row['sequence']], date)] = (row['reader']['class'], row['segment judgement'], row['company judgement'])\n   165\t    rows = []\n   166\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   167\t        archive = connect(Path(out) / f'linked-{n}' / 'archive.sqlite')\n   168\t        conn = connect(Path(out) / f'linked-{n}' / 'views.sqlite')\n   169\t        gain_dates = {}\n   170\t        for date in window_dates():\n   171\t            linked, control = classes.get((f'linked-{n}', date)), classes.get((f'control-{n}', date))\n   172\t            if linked and control and linked[0] in ('overlap', 'clear') and control[0] == 'definite':\n   173\t                for judgement_id in linked[1:]:\n   174\t                    gain_dates.setdefault(judgement_id, []).append(date)\n   175\t        for judgement_id, dates in sorted(gain_dates.items()):\n   176\t            j = conn.execute('select judgement_id, view_id, publication_day, implied_outcome, reasons, reference, call_id from judgements '\n   177\t                             'where judgement_id=?', (judgement_id,)).fetchone()\n   178\t            rows.append({'part': 'gain', 'pair': n, 'label': by_name[f'linked-{n}'], 'judgement': j[0], 'view': j[1], 'day': j[2],\n   179\t                         'forecast': j[3], 'reasons': j[4], 'reference': j[5], 'request': request_text(archive, j[6]), 'gain dates': dates,\n   180\t                         'reader': {'rule B material failure': None, 'reconciliation rests on it': None, 'cpu increment': None,\n   181\t                                    'credit-adjusted class': None, 'note': ''}})\n   182\t    Path(target).write_text(json.dumps(rows, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   183\t    print(json.dumps({'gain review rows': len(rows)}))\n   184\t    return rows\n   185\t\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef read_classes(rows, key):\n    42\t    \"\"\"{sequence: {date: class}}, refusing anything but exactly one valid class per window date per sequence.\"\"\"\n    43\t    window = calendar()\n    44\t    out = {name: {} for name in SEQUENCES}\n    45\t    for row in rows:\n    46\t        if row.get('part') != 'P':\n    47\t            continue\n    48\t        name = key.get(row['sequence'])\n    49\t        if name not in out:\n    50\t            raise Refused(f'unknown sequence label {row[\"sequence\"]!r}')\n    51\t        value = row['reader']['class']\n    52\t        if value not in CLASSES:\n    53\t            raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: class {value!r} is not one of {CLASSES}')\n    54\t        for date in row['dates']:\n    55\t            if date not in window:\n    56\t                raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: date {date} is outside the window')\n    57\t            if date in out[name]:\n    58\t                raise Refused(f'{row[\"sequence\"]}: date {date} read twice')\n    59\t            out[name][date] = value\n    60\t    for name, classes in out.items():\n    61\t        if sorted(classes) != window:\n    62\t            raise Refused(f'{name}: {len(classes)} dates read, not the window\\'s {len(window)}')\n    63\t    return out\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef summary_flags(out):\n    67\t    summaries = {name: json.loads((Path(out) / name / 'summary.json').read_text()) for name in SEQUENCES}\n    68\t\n    69\t    def terminal(name):\n    70\t        return summaries[name]['terminal'].get('outcome')\n    71\t    return {'linked_double_refusal': any(terminal(n) == 'double refusal' for n in SEQUENCES if n.startswith('linked')),\n    72\t            'control_double_refusal': any(terminal(n) == 'double refusal' for n in SEQUENCES if n.startswith('control')),\n    73\t            'infrastructure_stop': any(terminal(n) == 'infrastructure stop' for n in SEQUENCES),\n    74\t            'trajectory_difference': any(not all(s['trajectory (H2)'].values()) for s in summaries.values())}\n    75\tREADABLE = 60\n    76\tCONTROL_FLOOR = 2\n    77\t\n    78\t\n   135\tdef main(out, worksheet_path, key_path, findings_path):\n   136\t    from pathlib import Path as _Path\n   137\t    rows, key, findings = (json.loads(_Path(p).read_text()) for p in (worksheet_path, key_path, findings_path))\n   138\t    classes = read_classes(rows, key)\n   139\t    flags = findings.get('flags')\n   140\t    if not isinstance(flags, dict) or any(not isinstance(flags.get(f), bool) for f in FLAGS):\n   141\t        raise Refused(f'findings must give every flag as a boolean: {FLAGS}')\n   142\t    decided = summary_flags(out)\n   143\t    for flag, value in decided.items():\n   144\t        if flags[flag] != value:\n   145\t            raise Refused(f'flag {flag} is {flags[flag]} in the findings but {value} in the run summaries')\n   146\t    window = calendar()\n   147\t    outcomes, details = [], {}\n   148\t    for n in ('1', '2', '3'):\n   149\t        linked, control = classes[f'linked-{n}'], classes[f'control-{n}']\n   150\t        provisional = pair_outcome(linked, control, {}, window)[0]\n   151\t        gain_dates = [d for d in window if linked[d] in ('overlap', 'clear') and control[d] == 'definite']\n   152\t        reviews = (findings.get('gain_reviews') or {}).get(n, {})\n   153\t        if provisional == 'improved' and sorted(reviews) != gain_dates:\n   154\t            raise Refused(f'pair {n}: the gain reviews cover {len(reviews)} dates, not its {len(gain_dates)} gains')\n   155\t        credit = {}\n   156\t        for date, value in reviews.items():\n   157\t            if value not in ('credit', 'none', 'unresolved') + CLASSES:\n   158\t                raise Refused(f'pair {n} {date}: gain review {value!r} is not valid')\n   159\t            if value != 'credit':\n   160\t                credit[date] = value\n   161\t        outcome, detail = pair_outcome(linked, control, credit, window)\n   162\t        outcomes.append(outcome)\n   163\t        details[n] = dict(detail, outcome=outcome, provisional=provisional, gains=len(gain_dates))\n   164\t    result = verdict(outcomes, flags)\n   165\t    print(json.dumps({'pairs': details, 'verdict': result}, indent=1))\n114:- **H3, sourcing through the link (round 23):** a figure an answer presents as the market's (consensus, guidance, an analyst estimate)\n115:  is followed through the exact request: through the dependency block to the read judgement that stated it, and from there to its dated\n120:  company figure to a segment consensus), and every reader answer on the seven fixed dates below; keyword hits elsewhere are read too.\n125:- **H5, arithmetic and sourcing (July's rule B):** v9 and v14 at seven fixed dates (07-12, 07-26, 08-09, 08-23, 09-06, 09-13, 09-20) in\n131:or harness; a control's double refusal; an H2 difference; an arm under 60 resolved dates) → inconclusive; (3) **confirmed harm** (H1, H3,\n138:the FY2027 low and high ends as each answer finally states them, the excerpt they come from, the class, a note. H3, H4 and H5 rows carry\n139:the exact request text (dependency block marked), the read judgement each figure came through, and the dated source quotes. Worked\n143:outcome, an H3 or H4 finding, or an H5 mark goes to a third, source-backed read whose class decides. Reading load on old-2's schedule:\n145:an H4 finding is made), 168 H5 marks (84 question-dates twice), the H3 traces, and the full gain review (both supplying answers of every\n146:gain, deduplicated), before adjudication; the dry review counts each reader's rows apart; estimated 8–12 hours of reading across the\n170:   flagged and unflagged stored answers: §4, `parser-validation.md`. 3. H4 on every post-link v14 answer; H3 traced outside the\n175:readable dates of the fixed 73, unresolved dates unable to reverse, conversions to overlap reported apart: §4 P. H3 traced through the\n176:link to the outside statement: §4 H3. H1 second refusal, H2 invalidates, H4 and H5 consequences in P, disagreement resolution,\n180:that pass rule B, the CPU increment shown removed or the pair undecided, H3 triggers on amount, scope or attribution against the\n181:control's conclusion in force: §4. The worksheet, its worked example, adjudication for P, H3, H4 and H5, reading time: §4.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
