{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"'view_keys'|def _setting\\\" ../../../src/hivemind/views/store.py | head; nl -ba paid_run.py | sed -n '230,248p;337,368p'; nl -ba PAID-BUILD.md | sed -n '53,73p'\"","aggregated_output":"16:    'view_keys': 'view_id text primary key, measure text, scope text, scope_key text, period_start text, period_end text, basis text, unit text, event_type text, seq integer, scope_source text, key_version integer',\n110:    insert(conn, 'view_keys', view_id=view_id, measure=key['measure'], scope=key.get('scope', ''), scope_key=_universe.scope_key(key.get('scope', '')),\n   230\t                self.snapshot_checks += 1\n   231\t\n   232\t    def judge_day(self, original):\n   233\t        def wrapped(conn, archive_, cfg_, day, seq, **keywords):\n   234\t            before = archive_.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   235\t            self.day = day\n   236\t            try:\n   237\t                result = original(conn, archive_, cfg_, day, seq, **keywords)\n   238\t            finally:\n   239\t                self.day = None\n   240\t                after = archive_.conn.execute('select coalesce(max(call_id), 0) from model_calls').fetchone()[0]\n   241\t                self.day_windows[day] = (before, after)\n   242\t            failed = getattr(result, 'failed', None)\n   243\t            if failed and self.terminal is None:\n   244\t                text = str(failed)\n   245\t                view = text.split('judgement refused twice: ', 1)[1].split(':', 1)[0] if 'judgement refused twice: ' in text else None\n   246\t                self.terminal = ({'outcome': 'double refusal', 'view': view, 'day': day, 'reader': view in self.reader_days}\n   247\t                                 if view else {'outcome': 'infrastructure stop', 'day': day, 'reason': text[:300]})\n   248\t            return result\n   337\t    summary.update({\n   338\t        'terminal': run.terminal or {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   339\t        'links committed': committed,\n   340\t        'link jobs consumed': sorted(run.link_jobs),\n   341\t        'judge attempts at the transport': run.attempts,\n   342\t        'archive judge rows written (dated)': attempt_rows,\n   343\t        'stored refusals given back': run.refusals_given,\n   344\t        'reader judgements': reader_judgements,\n   345\t        'snapshot problems': run.snapshot_problems, 'snapshot checks': run.snapshot_checks,\n   346\t        'trajectory (H2)': trajectory_check(folder / 'views.sqlite', set(pinned['readers'])),\n   347\t        'latch': run.latch.reason, 'ledger': ledger_state(),\n   348\t    })\n   349\t    summary['acceptance'] = acceptance(summary, pinned, kind)\n   350\t    (folder / 'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   351\t    return summary\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\tdef acceptance(summary, pinned, kind):\n   355\t    \"\"\"The one gate for the dry runs and the paid send.\"\"\"\n   356\t    judgements = summary['reader judgements']\n   357\t    checks = {\n   358\t        'window completed, no stop': summary['stopped'] == '' and summary['terminal'] == {'outcome': 'complete'},\n   359\t        'committed graph equals the pinned one (labels included)': summary['links committed'] == (pinned['graph'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   360\t        'probe jobs consumed exactly the pinned set': summary['link jobs consumed'] == (pinned['probe jobs'] if kind == 'linked' else []),\n   361\t        'every post-link reader judgement fresh on its own day': all(j['fresh on its day'] for j in judgements if j['must be fresh']),\n   362\t        'every pre-link reader judgement from the archive': all(j['from the archive'] for j in judgements if not j['must be fresh']),\n   363\t        'reader judgements present': bool(judgements),\n   364\t        'upstream snapshot clean': not summary['snapshot problems'],\n   365\t        'upstream snapshot exercised (linked)': kind == 'control' or summary['snapshot checks'] > 0,\n   366\t        'fixed trajectory (H2)': all(summary['trajectory (H2)'].values()),\n   367\t    }\n   368\t    return dict(checks, accepted=all(checks.values()))\n    53\t   `preflight-window.log` (old-2's archive and ledger) and `v120-replay-{1,2,3}.log` (the probe archives' link answers).\n    54\t4. **The worksheet and the verdict:** `worksheet.py build` writes P rows under shuffled labels (key outside the repository) and H rows\n    55\t   with the exact requests, the read judgement ids shown and the paired control's conclusion in force (H4), the seven fixed dates (H5),\n    56\t   and reference changes or market-figure keywords (H3); `worksheet.py gains` writes the gain review rows after P is read (both linked\n    57\t   answers per gain, deduplicated). `verdict.py` refuses: off-window dates, a date read twice or missing, a class outside the four, a\n    58\t   missing or non-boolean flag, a missing or invalid gain review for a provisionally improved pair, and a run-decided flag that disagrees\n    59\t   with the six summaries (`worksheet-verdict-dry.log`: a synthetic reading of the dry stores gives \"pass\"; each of six bad inputs is\n    60\t   refused).\n    61\t\n    62\t## Rerun evidence ($0)\n    63\t- `paid-dry-{linked,control}-{1,2,3}.log`: all six accepted by the gate; 266 / 247 bought; 266 snapshot checks per linked sequence.\n    64\t- `paid-dry-refused-upstream.log`: accepted, 267 bought, the refused answer shown to no request.\n    65\t- `paid-mutant-{1..6}.log`, each refused by the gate on its named check: control not retired (freshness), stale upstream recorded and\n    66\t  swapped upstreams (snapshot), a reader missing from the allow-list and a probe answer missing (window not completed), a non-reader\n    67\t  bought (H2, now in the summary itself).\n    68\t- `verdict-checks.log` (14), `paid-units.log` (3), `worksheet-verdict-dry.log`.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Reading load, measured on the dry worksheet\n    71\tP 432 rows; H4 213; H5 84; H3 1,521 in the dry run, an upper bound (every marker answer changes its reference); a real run's H3 count\n    72\tis known only after the run. Gain rows 18 in the synthetic reading.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import worksheet as w\nfrom pathlib import Path\ndry=next(Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/scratchpad/paid-dry2/linked-1/summary.json'\\\\'')).parent.parent\nimport json\nmissing=[]\nfor n in w.SEQUENCES:\n folder=dry/n\n conn=w.connect(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n rows=w.h_rows(dry,n,'\\\\''S-Z'\\\\'')\n indexed={(r['\\\\''view'\\\\''],r['\\\\''judgement'\\\\'']) for r in rows if r['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''H3'\\\\''}\n starts=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''reader days'\\\\'']\n for view in w.READERS:\n  for date in w.FIXED_DATES:\n   j=w.in_force(w.judgements(conn,view),date)\n   if j and j[1]>=starts[view] and (view,j[0]) not in indexed:missing.append((n,view,date,j[1]))\nprint('\\\\''fixed-date H3 records absent'\\\\'',len(missing),missing)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import worksheet as w\nfrom pathlib import Path\ndry=next(Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/scratchpad/paid-dry2/linked-1/summary.json'\\\\'')).parent.parent\nimport json\nmissing=[]\nfor n in w.SEQUENCES:\n folder=dry/n\n conn=w.connect(folder/'\\\\''views.sqlite'\\\\'')\n rows=w.h_rows(dry,n,'\\\\''S-Z'\\\\'')\n indexed={(r['\\\\''view'\\\\''],r['\\\\''judgement'\\\\'']) for r in rows if r['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''H3'\\\\''}\n starts=json.loads((folder/'\\\\''summary.json'\\\\'').read_text())['\\\\''reader days'\\\\'']\n for view in w.READERS:\n  for date in w.FIXED_DATES:\n   j=w.in_force(w.judgements(conn,view),date)\n   if j and j[1]>=starts[view] and (view,j[0]) not in indexed:missing.append((n,view,date,j[1]))\nprint('\\\\''fixed-date H3 records absent'\\\\'',len(missing),missing)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"fixed-date H3 records absent 6 [('linked-1', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26'), ('linked-2', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26'), ('linked-3', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26'), ('control-1', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26'), ('control-2', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26'), ('control-3', 'v21', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-26')]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The rebuild closes several round-28 gaps, but I reproduced two false passes: one using a sequence the acceptance gate rejected, and another with no completed harm or gain-judgement reviews.\n\n### What holds as fixed\n\n`send` now uses the same acceptance gate as `dry`. The gate compares the labelled graph and exact probe hashes, and checks freshness against each judgement day’s archive window. The judging-day scope clears on exit, and a title alone can no longer admit a request. H2 uses the pinned reader set, so the non-reader purchase mutant now fails in its own summary. The stale and swapped upstream mutants are caught, and the logs show typed outcomes for double refusals in both arms and a reservation refusal with zero spend. [Admission](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:156) · [Acceptance gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:354) · [Rerun evidence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:48)\n\n### Blocking findings\n\n1. **Carry the acceptance decision through to the verdict.** I substituted the actual no-retirement mutant’s summary for `control-1`. Its gate says `accepted: false`, but the verdict still returned **pass** because it reads the terminal outcome and H2 and ignores the failed freshness check. The paid gate itself also accepts a completed summary with `ledger.stopped` and `ledger.overrun` both true. Require the exact completed window and a clean final ledger, and require all six accepted summaries for an ordinary comparison. Evaluate terminal outcomes before requiring the full P worksheet. I confirmed that a linked double refusal with missing P rows currently raises a coverage error instead of returning the prescribed **fail**. [Paid gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:337) · [Rejected mutant](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid-mutant-1.log:6) · [Verdict handoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:66) · [Verdict entry point](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:135)\n2. **Require the underlying reviews, not just their conclusions.** Exact dates, duplicate rows, invalid classes, missing flags, and missing gain *dates* are now checked. I still got **pass** with P rows only, all harm booleans set to false, and `credit` entered per gain date. No H3–H5 row or review of either supplying judgement was required. Validate completed and adjudicated reviews against the worksheet’s expected judgement IDs. Derive H1 from the dated attempts and derive gain credit from the two supplying reviews. Add the P-only false pass and the rejected-summary case to the end-to-end checks. [Gain rows](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:154) · [Verdict inputs](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:135)\n3. **Finish the reading packets.** P labels are shuffled, but H rows in the same file contain the label and the real arm name. I recovered all six mappings without the key. Give the blind reader a separate packet. H3 also omits the paired control conclusion in force and does not explicitly include the seven fixed dates. I found **six missing H3 entries** in the dry stores: `v21` on July 26 in each sequence. Include those fixed-date rows, and give readers a trace from each linked figure through the supplying judgement to its dated outside source. [H-row construction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:99) · [Packet assembly](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:136) · [Pinned H3 and reading rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:114)\n\n**H3 workload needs to be settled before sending.** Applying the current filter to real old-2 answers selected **244 of 247** reader judgements, about **1,464 rows** across six similar sequences. The dry count of 1,521 is therefore a realistic workload estimate. Time a representative batch of source traces, account for adjudication, and pin how an identical source trace may be reused while retaining a finding for every required occurrence. The verdict must require that work to be complete. [H3 filter](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:123) · [Dry workload](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-BUILD.md:70)\n\n**$7 remains a reasonable ceiling to propose** after these fixes, against the **$5.89** planning estimate. It leaves room for the projected reservations and some variation in spend. A ceiling stop remains inconclusive. [Price estimate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/price.log:70)"}}
